{"note": "The COMPLETE case-site policy: the twin of `cases-policy.json` for `source: \"monoExtension\"`, which walks the compiler's own mono declaration list and so also reaches `f._redArg`, `f._lam_N` and friends. SEEDED from a measured scan (`--seed-policy`); it is a PIN, not a proof. Regenerate the seed and diff; never overwrite a note. REMOVED 2026-09-10 (idiomatic pass, audit seat): the rule for `Effect4.Program.compileEff` on `Effect4.Program.NativeOp`. That case site was never in the source — the compiler created it by specialising `NativeOp.row` at `.external` — and at `ae85bd6` the compiled code no longer has it, with NO change under src/ between the two commits (`git diff dba71eb..ae85bd6 -- src/` is empty). A case-site count is a count of compiler output read out of a BUILD DIRECTORY, so a gate must build `Effect4` before it scans. If the compiler creates the site again, `unlisted: refuse` catches it as one named row, which is the behaviour this policy wants.",
